<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49301" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trŭcīdātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		trucido, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a slaughtering</i>, <i>massacring</i>, <i>butchery.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inde non jam pugna, sed trucidatio velut
					pecorum fleri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					28, 16, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 4, 5, 11</span></i>
			.—In <i>plur. absol.</i>: tantas
			trucidationes facis, Cato ap. <i><span class="en">Gell. 13,
				24, 12</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a cutting to
			pieces</i>, <i>cutting up</i>, <i>cutting off</i>, Cels. praef. <i>med.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">arborum,</span>”
				<i>a lopping</i>, <i>trimming</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					17, 27, 45, § 257</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
